&lt;p&gt;Senior Product Manager&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; UK (remote)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reachdesk is the first truly end-to-end global SaaS gifting and swag platform, helping B2B companies create meaningful connections with prospects, customers, and employees, while driving measurable ROI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe gifting is more than just a transaction: it’s about building genuine human connections that fuel business growth. Whether it’s engaging prospects, celebrating customers, or recognizing employees, our platform makes it easy to deliver personalized gifts, branded swag, and unforgettable event &amp;amp; brand experiences at scale through automated sourcing, storage, and global delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trusted by many of the most recognized names in technology and SaaS, Reachdesk integrates effortlessly with marketing, sales, and HRIS tech stacks and is powered by our world-class team across New York, London, and Lisbon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re growing, and we’re currently looking for a Senior Product Manager to join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Manager at Reachdesk, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the Reachdesk Platform. You will be accountable for turning complex customer and business problems into software products that deliver measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Chief Product Officer, you’ll lead product initiatives end-to-end,&amp;nbsp; from identifying and deeply understanding the right problems to solve, through discovery and delivery, to launch, adoption, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll operate with a high degree of autonomy, proactively building context across customers, the market, internal stakeholders, data, and technology to understand what Reachdesk needs to achieve its goals. You’ll also make sound decisions when the path forward isn’t obvious.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll partner closely with Engineering and Design and work across the wider business to create alignment, communicate decisions clearly, and ensure what we build is successfully launched, adopted, and delivers the outcomes we set out to achieve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy solving difficult problems, taking ownership, and moving comfortably between customer, technical, and business conversations, you’ll thrive in this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set product direction and priorities&lt;/strong&gt;, bringing together company goals, internal stakeholder needs, customer insight, market context, data, and technical considerations to focus on the highest-impact opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define problems and experiences before solutions&lt;/strong&gt;, creating clear stories, journeys, and shared context so the Design and Engineering teams understand the problem and intended outcomes before determining the solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead product initiatives end-to-end&lt;/strong&gt;, from discovery and solution definition through delivery, rollout, and iteration, partnering with Engineering to manage scope, make pragmatic trade-offs, and deliver valuable solutions at pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make sound product decisions and trade-offs&lt;/strong&gt;, balancing customer and business needs, commercial impact, user experience, and technical considerations while aligning the wider business on compromises, priorities, and expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop product opportunities with external partners&lt;/strong&gt;, building relationships with technology partners to uncover mutual opportunities, shape integrations, align roadmaps, and navigate the product and commercial considerations required to bring them to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Orchestrate successful launches and adoption&lt;/strong&gt;, working across Sales, Marketing, Customer Success, Services, Logistics, Finance, Legal, and other teams to ensure the business is ready and customers realise value from what we build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communicate with clarity throughout&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring leadership and teams across Reachdesk understand product decisions, progress, risks, changes, and results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong track record of &lt;strong&gt;owning B2B SaaS products end-to-end&lt;/strong&gt;, from identifying the right problems through delivery, adoption, and measurable customer and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a &lt;strong&gt;strong problem solver&lt;/strong&gt; who gets to the root of complex problems, brings structure to ambiguity, and uses evidence and judgement to determine the right path forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You operate with &lt;strong&gt;independence and initiative&lt;/strong&gt;: you seek out the customers, stakeholders, data, and context you need rather than waiting for direction, while staying anchored to Reachdesk’s goals and priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have &lt;strong&gt;strong business and commercial awareness&lt;/strong&gt; and are curious about how the wider company operates, allowing you to understand competing needs and make pragmatic decisions beyond the boundaries of Product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re &lt;strong&gt;technically fluent enough to work effectively with Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;, understand systems, integrations, and constraints, ask the right questions, and contribute meaningfully to solution and scope decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an &lt;strong&gt;exceptional communicator&lt;/strong&gt;, able to create clarity, influence decisions, surface difficult trade-offs, and adapt how you communicate across customers, engineers, leadership, and teams throughout the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable &lt;strong&gt;operating externally as well as internally&lt;/strong&gt;, building productive relationships with technology partners, uncovering shared opportunities, influencing without authority, and navigating product, technical, and commercial conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong sense of &lt;strong&gt;product and user experience&lt;/strong&gt;, caring about the coherence and quality of the complete experience rather than whether individual requirements or features have simply been delivered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary with generous stock options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension with employer contributions (NEST)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Affordable Private Medical Insurance, including mental health support and fast access to care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO that increases the longer you’re with us, plus extra flexibility for life’s unexpected moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuinely collaborative culture with innovative, fun, and ambitious people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reachdesk believes that a diverse team helps us achieve our mission faster, and so we welcome applicants from all backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Privacy Policy: We process personal information submitted as part of your application in accordance with the Reachdesk Candidate Privacy Notice. Please review Reachdesk’s Privacy Policy here: &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.reachdesk.com/candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;www.reachdesk.com/candidate-privacy-policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message skipProofing&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience Without Limits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come shape the future of brand experience.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message skipProofing&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Jack Morton, we design and build&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;head-turning, smile-inducing, impact-driving brand experiences that redefine what experiential marketing can achieve. We help our clients&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;unlock the full value of experiences&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;by turning bold ideas into meaningful connections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message skipProofing&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;That takes a team that&#39;s bold, curious, and acts as one.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We build on each other&#39;s ideas, challenge conventions, and show up for one another every day. Here, you&#39;ll do your best work, grow quickly, and partner across clients, disciplines, and global teams to bring new ideas to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message skipProofing&quot;&gt;This is a place where curiosity drives what’s next, boldness raises the bar, and every win is shared. Where ownership is expected, egos are left at the door, and the work reflects the passion and talent of the people behind it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message skipProofing&quot;&gt;Experience without limits—in your work, your growth, and your impact.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Account Director is responsible for leading a portfolio of client accounts, acting as the senior strategic partner and primary point of contact. This role drives the overall client relationship, ensuring delivery excellence, commercial performance, and long-term growth. The Account Director will translate client objectives into innovative event strategies, lead cross-functional teams, and maintain the highest standards of service, promote creativity, and profitability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Relationship &amp;amp; Strategic Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own, develop, and execute strategic relationship plans for Executive Leadership, C-Suite, and key stakeholders across assigned accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted advisor to clients, providing strategic counsel, insight, and creative innovation that supports their business objectives and elevates partnership value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the creation and execution of robust client retention and growth strategies, ensuring year-on-year account stability and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement tailored business development plans within existing client portfolios, identifying opportunities for new services and revenue streams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion the agency’s full-service offering, ensuring amplification services (digital, creative, production, engagement, etc.) are effectively positioned and integrated into client solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial &amp;amp; Financial Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the financial performance of allocated accounts, including revenue forecasting, gross margin delivery, and profitability targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the commercial review process, ensuring accurate pricing models, transparent financial tracking, and proactive margin management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive commercial excellence through regular analysis of client profitability, resource utilisation, and pricing initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure internal CRMs, budgets, and commercial documentation are accurate, complete, and aligned with internal governance standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Delivery &amp;amp; Quality Assurance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee delivery of all client Service Level Agreements (SLAs) and Key Performance Indicators (KPIs), ensuring standards of excellence across all programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide senior oversight of project/account management teams to ensure projects are delivered on time, on budget, and to the highest compliance and quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal operations, compliance, and delivery teams to maintain robust governance frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Quarterly Business Reviews (QBRs) to evaluate performance against KPIs, identify areas for improvement, and shape future strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New Business &amp;amp; RFP Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In partnership with New Business Development, lead the strategic response and delivery of RFPs, proposals, and pitch presentations for assigned accounts and support new opportunities that IXM receive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development of thought leadership, case studies, and credentials that reinforce the agency’s expertise within the LifeSciences sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, mentor and coach all direct reports ensuring monthly meetings to discuss progress and review development plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the development, mentoring and coaching of the wider team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with the Associate Director Talent Management, monitor development plans for all team members considering:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current skills analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training needs analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Individual’s needs and desires&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Development planning strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead on recruitment process, interviewing and selecting new team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide consistent leadership, motivation and direction to all team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Executive Leadership to ensure all teams are consistently sharing best practice and delivering to Impact-XM standards at all times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Management of direct report holidays and lieu days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the management of wider team holidays and lieu days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;General&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and review timesheet activity in Company time sheet system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare monthly client project analysis to ensure team and recruitment costs are assessed against client budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 8–10 years’ experience in client services, account management, or event strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of managing global or multi-market client portfolios and developing long-term senior stakeholder relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial acumen, with demonstrable experience in budget management, margin optimisation, and pricing strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth understanding of industry compliance and regulatory frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading multi-disciplinary teams and fostering collaboration across operations, creative, digital, and production functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional presentation, negotiation, and communication skills with the ability to influence at senior levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker with a proactive approach to identifying opportunities for growth, innovation, and service excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Last but not least, we believe in diversity, equity and inclusion.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jack Morton is an equal opportunity employer; we strongly value diversity at our companies. We do not discriminate on race, religion, color, national origin, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, veteran status, or any other basis prohibited by law.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;#LI-XXX&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Requisition #: 2099&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;We make our careers website accessible to any and all users. If you need an accommodation to participate in the application process, please contact us at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ---------- &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;This email address is not for general employment inquiries or vendors; rather it is strictly for applicants who require special assistance accessing our employment website. Due to volume, messages sent to this email address that are not related to an accommodation cannot be answered.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
